IX. The Financial Transaction Dividend

America has an enormous financial system.

A tiny fee applied to certain financial transactions could generate revenue without requiring a large percentage tax on ordinary household activity.

Conceptually:

R_f=\tau\times V

where:

* \tau = transaction fee
* V = taxable transaction volume

Even a very small \tau can produce substantial revenue if V is enormous.

The key design problem would be avoiding excessive disruption to productive investment while targeting high-volume speculative activity where policymakers choose to do so.

