The Alaska experience is relevant here. Research examining its permanent dividend found no significant reduction in aggregate employment and found an increase in part-time employment, consistent with the possibility that broad cash transfers stimulate local economic activity. 

That does not prove that a nationwide UBI would have identical effects; Alaska is a very different economy. But it provides an empirical case worth studying.

