XV. Mathematical Guardrails

A credible UBI system cannot simply promise unlimited payments.

It requires fiscal equations.

One possible rule:

UBI_t=\min(B_{target},\frac{R_t+\alpha F_t}{N_t})

where:

* B_{target} = target annual benefit
* R_t = current dedicated revenue
* F_t = fund value
* \alpha = sustainable distribution rate
* N_t = population

This creates an automatic fiscal stabilizer.

When revenue rises:

UBI\uparrow

When revenue falls:

UBI\downarrow

within predetermined boundaries.

The government therefore cannot casually promise a payment that its revenue system cannot support.

