XVII. The Endgame: America as a Shareholding Society

The deepest version of the idea is not simply UBI.

It is Universal Basic Ownership.

Instead of asking:

“How much redistribution can the government afford?”

the country asks:

“What assets should every American have a claim upon?”

That could include a diversified national portfolio of:

* natural resources
* public land
* infrastructure
* intellectual property
* spectrum
* carbon permits
* financial assets
* public enterprises
* AI-related economic rents
* data-related revenues

The government becomes less like a household distributing its paycheck and more like a trustee managing a gigantic national endowment.

Alaska demonstrates a version of this philosophy: resource wealth is converted into an investment fund, and the resulting financial earnings support dividends and public purposes. 

